## 5) Wire it up (one place)

Create: `halo/HaloDefaultRegistry.kt`

```kotlin
package halo

import halo.core.PluginRegistry
import halo.plugins.IChingPlugin
import halo.plugins.TarotMajorPlugin
import halo.plugins.RunesPlugin
import halo.plugins.NumerologyElementalPlugin

fun defaultRegistry(): PluginRegistry =
    PluginRegistry()
        .register(IChingPlugin())
        .register(TarotMajorPlugin())
        .register(RunesPlugin())
        .register(NumerologyElementalPlugin())
```

Usage (anywhere, e.g., ViewModel):

```kotlin
import halo.core.*
import halo.defaultRegistry
import halo.core.HaloEngine

val engine = HaloEngine(defaultRegistry())

val req = OracleRequest(
    question = "What’s my clean next move?",
    seed = 906L,
    dice = DiceRoll(sides = 20, values = listOf(7, 18, 3, 19)),
    tolerance = ToleranceMode.FORGIVING
)

val resp = engine.run(req)
// resp.synthesis.headline / body + resp.results for plugin cards
```

